A||N||17||NOS3800||Williamsburg Best of Show not worthy||||9||
Z||000000||NOS3800||08-06-2001||09:48 PM||||All those that attended the Williamsburg Show know that I won the Best of Show and the Peoples Choice awards. I want to be the first to say that I do not feel I deserved these awards. I feel there may have been an error, there were enough of them over the weekend. I feel that either Chris Moore or my brothers SC 3800 car were more deserving. I mean, I got thrid place in my class. How does a third place car win Best of Show?<BR>Anyway, I just want everyone to know I wasn't happy with the results, and I felt that the judging in the modified classes was awfully strict. I do not understand how I got third out of the three cars present. I agree that Chris Moore deserved the first place trophy that he finally recieved. I have beaten him at both Carlisle events, and each time felt his was the better car. <BR>Also, SkiTime also deserved a trophy also. His car was clean and just do not understand how he didn't get a trophy.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||9
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||08-06-2001||10:27 PM||||I think your purple GT deserved Best of Show - I definitely do. Damn, I mean, did you get the seats covered first and then match the paint to the seats? That car was awesome. Just friggin' cool as Hell. <P>I *did* think that they should have split the awards so that they were distributed a little bit more... my vote for People's Choice went to Skitime, but it wasn't a slight against you - it was because Skitime had ideas that were things I'd love to do to mine if I had the skill and the balls to try them. <P>Chris Moore's car was/is AWESOME - Hell, it was the Automoda convertable conversion kit that was partially responsible for me getting my first Fiero back in 1990 and hooking me for life. Ironically, Automoda went out of business before I could afford to convert the car I bought specifically for the task, but c'est la vie... but he already got more than one *very* well-deserved awards this year, so I don't think he's hurtin' much.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The awards ceremony definitely was a bit goofed up at times - like the sheets reflecting ZERO Indy Pace Cars registered, when we all damn well knew there was one in the running, so that kinda made some of us wonder what else may have been amiss, but I definitely don't think that you winning Best of Show was a screwup or a fluke - you earned it. <P>Kudos to you, your car, and your humility. I'm raising a beer to you right now as I type this. <P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||08-06-2001||10:33 PM||||NOS3800, without a doubt your car is awesome. I don't understand the placement in your class but I think that best of show is voted by all the judges not just the judge in your class. So obviously the rest of the judges choose your car. So be proud of your trophy, you do deserve it. Now as you know I am new to showing, as this is my first season and maybe don't understand the judging correctly but I think your car did deserve your best of show.<P>Thanks for the kind words on my car but I guess I need to work on it more according to my judge. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||NOS3800||08-06-2001||11:39 PM||||I did not relly understand the judging either. Usually, I would think the judging would be left to the STOCK classes, because they are harder to compare. I am not knocking the system, I just was ready for it. I mean they were taking off points for any orange peel, the famous scratches in the side windows( they made us put the passenger window up)and they crawled under the cars. I glimpsed my brothers score sheet while they were judging it, and he got 1.5 points for the dash. 1.5 points????? There isn't much wrong with his dash. It was just TOO strict. These cars are mostly daily drivers, My brothers and mine are driven EVERY DAY. It s hard to get ready for a show as it is, but when I wasn't expecting such thorough judging I was just flat out shocked. Especially when the car that got second had cracked door panels among other things. I just didn't think it was fair. <BR>Anyway, this was my first FOCOA show and I found it enjoyable. The people were VERY nice, especially Gloria. I loved seeing cars I have never seen before( I usually attend the shows in the MD,PA area). Some that stood out( sorry I didn't get names) The orange GT that won best non GM paint was beautiful. Also, the bright yellow GT with chrome rims and I believe a turbo. ALSO, I loved the yellow coupe( tweety Bird) I believe it was at Carlisle also. BEautiful car and it did well in a difficult class considering it had the 4 in it. Thats always a obstacle in a MOD class.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||08-06-2001||11:57 PM||||Ive been showing cars for 30 years. One thing ive found is theres never ever any sense to be made of judging. I just enjoy showing my car and talking with everyone, dont really care about the trophy thing myself anymore. I went to one show and got 1st place with a 100 point score, did another show by same people and got second to a VW Thing. Just enjoy what you get. I too have seen cars that were gorgeous and got nothing and junk cars that won. <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||MooCow||08-07-2001||12:14 AM||||Can I see some pics of your car NOS3800??<BR>Wish I could have went.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||5
Z||000006||NOS3800||08-07-2001||12:28 AM||||Here is my webpage since I haven't figured out how to put a pick here yet.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/bills3800" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/bills3800</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||6
Z||000007||artherd||08-07-2001||04:22 AM||||OH WOW!  Nos, I just saw pics of your car for the first time (Haven't had the pleasure in person; yet :)  All I can say is I know why you won.  <P>It's that good 'ol checkered tarp :) (no really, your paint is drop-dead-make-grown-men-cry georgous.  Really.  And the seats just top it, how did you do them?!?!<P>Your car just makes me say "heck yes!!!" out loud.  (Chris, so does your northstar Automoda top GT :)<P>A tough call, but I can see how any of you could win best of show.   Perhaps there should have been a tie?<P>Anyway, the shows aren't about the judging (for me) but about getting together and meeting other nutcases :)<P>I mean Fiero lovers.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000008||FIERO JOHN-WI||08-07-2001||08:39 AM||||I have been to many FOCOA Nationals and have been a judge, 3 different times and I truely agree that the judging wrong.I would say that 98.9% of all custom fieros are driven, nobdy wants to stick tons of money customizing it not to drive it, basically as a judge for the judge class we are mainly suppoesed to look at how clean the car is period! Yeah we do get only 1 question asking how does the over all modification look but thats it. I always thought that the stock cars should be judge because they are so identical and how really clean would come into play, but custom /modified/semi mod and so on should be judge by other people in their class because they know the work that goes into it, now as for when I judge the class I took this to heart because I had a semi-mod car(yellow convertible Gt) so I just thought I would give my 2 cents!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||08-07-2001||09:29 AM||||Dude, your car was awesome, and while I did vote for Skitime for People's Choice, you also were very deserving of the People's Choice award.  I was a bit confused how Best of Show can be awarded to anyone other than a 1st place car.  How can you win Best of Show if someone else beat you in your class?  <P>Still - it's an awesome car and you deserved the recognition.  ||||reg||6
