Z||000011||Jaygee79||08-07-2001||11:26 AM||||Are we talking about the same one that was at Carlisle?  If so then you definitely deserve Best Of Show.  Be proud of yourself and your car!  That is one beautiful Fiero.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooh14.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Pontiaddict||08-07-2001||11:49 AM||||I'm not a fan of purple cars, but I have to say, that is some nice paint.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/pasig.gif">       <BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><FONT SIZE="1">"The most successful American mid-engine car ever built"</FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000013||dlancer407||08-07-2001||10:09 PM||||NOS3800; Your car looks fantastic! I agree with RogerGarrason. I have been showing cars since 1985. Over the years there have been many times when I thought how did that car beat me? On the other hand there have been times when I had to think Wow I really got lucky today. Relax and enjoy your victory. Over the years it all evens out.<P><BR>dlancer407<BR>1985 GT Coupe<BR>black & silver||||reg||12
Z||000014||8Ball||08-07-2001||10:54 PM||||NOS, Do you have anymore pics of the interior? I absolutly loved what I could see.<BR>I ahve always wanted and purple and black int. although I want more purple than black  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Randy<P>------------------<BR>The Fieroless Fiero Nut||||reg||1
Z||000015||NOS3800||08-07-2001||11:03 PM||||Those that are wondering about my interior, they are Mr. Mikes seats. They are done in vinyl, cause it was cheaper($280) as opposed to $380 for leather and purple isn't availible in leather. The car is a daily driver, so if I did happen to tear a cover it would be cheaper to replace. Everything you need to replace the covers come with the kit, even a video to help you. It was very simple to do. The seats match the car almost perfectly in person, they look more pinkish in the pics over the net.<BR>The color of the dash and such was changed using a spray die. It was VERY simple and worked great. The headliner was done with a headliner repair kit from Pep Boys for 30 bucks. Carpet and floor mats with purple"GT" logo were obtained from ACC carpets.<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000016||Dragon||08-07-2001||11:11 PM||||NOS3800 <P>   You have a great looking car.  In regards to how it made Best Of Show - It was well worth consideration.  <P>------------------<BR>Dragon<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://spacecoastfieros.com/dragon.jpg">  <P>   Space Coast Fieros||||reg||14
Z||000017||TWEETIE BIRD||08-07-2001||11:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NOS3800:<BR><B>I did not relly understand the judging either. Usually, I would think the judging would be left to the STOCK classes, because they are harder to compare. I am not knocking the system, I just was ready for it. I mean they were taking off points for any orange peel, the famous scratches in the side windows( they made us put the passenger window up)and they crawled under the cars. I glimpsed my brothers score sheet while they were judging it, and he got 1.5 points for the dash. 1.5 points????? There isn't much wrong with his dash. It was just TOO strict. These cars are mostly daily drivers, My brothers and mine are driven EVERY DAY. It s hard to get ready for a show as it is, but when I wasn't expecting such thorough judging I was just flat out shocked. Especially when the car that got second had cracked door panels among other things. I just didn't think it was fair. <BR>Anyway, this was my first FOCOA show and I found it enjoyable. The people were VERY nice, especially Gloria. I loved seeing cars I have never seen before( I usually attend the shows in the MD,PA area). Some that stood out( sorry I didn't get names) The orange GT that won best non GM paint was beautiful. Also, the bright yellow GT with chrome rims and I believe a turbo. ALSO, I loved the yellow coupe( tweety Bird) I believe it was at Carlisle also. BEautiful car and it did well in a difficult class considering it had the 4 in it. Thats always a obstacle in a MOD class.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thank you so much for the compliment. I have worked very hard getting it to look the way it does now. I also won 1st place last year at the Nationals, but don't do very well in other shows. I only got third in Carlisle. <BR>This car was headed for the junk yard when I <BR>tried to revive it. It's different working with a used abused car than working with a fairly new car. I still continue to make changes and improvements that I can. Thanks again, you made my day! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||10
